WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.778
Ship your Godot game to WeChat, Douyin, and TikTok mini games, in one click.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.592
Until now, that meant custom engine builds, broken templates, and glue code.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.840
Now, one panel does it all.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.013
Pick a platform, enter your App ID, click Export.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:25.287
You get the game pack, a mini-game engine, adapters, and platform config. No Node.js, no Emscripten.

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:34.862
Open the folder in the platform's DevTools. The engine is built for mini games: single-threaded, no SIMD, no WebAssembly exceptions.

7
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:43.255
Then call mini-game features straight from GDScript: two hundred and twenty-five methods and eighty-four signals, across all three hosts.

8
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.707
Every template matches your exact Godot version, and certified templates download, verify, and install in one click.

9
00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.134
Zero extra tools. Three platforms. One Godot project.

10
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.120
Godot Mini Game is free and open source. Find it on GitHub.
